{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/09 15:20 SAST
Version: 0.7
Description:
  The weighted tag cloud: every label in the catalogue, sized by how much of it each one holds.

  A partial rather than markup on the tag page because the catalogue draws the same control. The
  rail beside the course grid narrows what is already on screen; this is how a reader finds a
  subject at all, and the two must not be different controls wearing the same name.

  The caller supplies cloud_tags and, optionally, cloud_limit - the catalogue shows the heaviest
  tags rather than all of them, because the whole taxonomy is a page of its own.
Changelog:
  2026/09/09 15:20 SAST
  - Extracted from pages/course-tags.html.twig so the catalogue can render the same cloud.
#}
{% set shown = cloud_limit is defined and cloud_limit ? cloud_tags|slice(0, cloud_limit) : cloud_tags %}
{% if shown %}
	<div class="cl-tag-cloud">
		{% for cloud_tag in shown %}
			<a class="cl-tag-chip cl-tag-weight-{{ cloud_tag.weight }}" href="/courses/tag/{{ cloud_tag.slug }}{{ universe_query|default('') }}"
			   title="{{ cloud_tag.name }}">{% if cloud_tag.icon_svg is defined and cloud_tag.icon_svg %}<span class="cl-tag-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ cloud_tag.icon_svg|raw }}</span>{% endif %}<span>{{ cloud_tag.name }}</span>
			<span class="cl-category-count">{{ cloud_tag.course_count }}</span>
			</a>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
{% endif %}
